  "instructor": [
    {
      "text": "Welcome to the Integration Capstone. This is the final test: build one quadcopter that satisfies the whole mission at once — everything you learned in Experiments 1 to 10 has to agree.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Read the Mission Brief on the left: a maximum all-up weight, a minimum flight time, and a payload the aircraft must lift. Every choice you make will be judged against all three together.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Tap any component tile to open its option library. The subsystems are coupled — a bigger motor lifts more but draws more current, heats the ESC and drains the battery faster. Watch the live metrics react.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Tick the payload box to load the mission cargo, then read Mission Verify on the right: weight, thrust-to-weight, hover throttle, flight time, ESC temperature and hover efficiency all update as you build.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "When you think it is ready, press Verify Build. If any constraint fails, the result names only the experiment whose concept you have not yet applied — no shortcut. Return to it, rebuild, and verify again.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Clear every constraint at once and the aircraft is flight-verified. That single build is the proof that the ten prior concepts have become one working design.",
      "audio": null
    }
  ],
  "reward": {
    "category": null,
    "name": "Showdown",
    "desc": "The capstone is the final verification run — there is nothing left to unlock."
  }
